Object.assign(ENEMIES,{
 xian:{name:"Madam Xian, the Ninth Reel",hp:52,p2at:20,allies:true,
  open:"She sets down her teacup on the convening-hall floor, precisely, and rises, and the mulberry sweetness opens onto the vast patient thing it always wrapped. \u201CI have hosted you with my whole heart, weaver. The Lady may gamble four hundred years on your arithmetic. I tithe to this Loom \u2014 I am IN the sky you propose to take down and retie. Forgive me. The hostess will resume when one of us yields.\u201D",
  p2text:"Something in her lets go of being seemly. The tithe-lines reverse all at once, four decades of paid-in self flooding home, and Madam Xian becomes, briefly, what she has been quietly financing all along.",
  moves:[{n:"Silk Court Form",kind:"stance",st:"flow",text:"She moves the way the white boat moved: poured, seamless, nothing to grip.",tele:"Her form is pouring \u2014 white-boat water, nothing to hold."},
   {n:"Needle-script",d:6,drain:2},
   {n:"Drawing the tithe",kind:"heal",h:6,text:"Her outward filaments brighten \u2014 she draws back a measure of forty years\u2019 paid-in self, and her edges reknit.",tele:"Her filaments brighten \u2014 she is about to draw on her own tithe."},
   {n:"Winding the Ninth",kind:"charge",text:"Every reel in the hall turns toward her at once, thread gathering on her sleeves like storm-light.",tele:"The hall\u2019s reels feed her \u2014 the Ninth\u2019s seal-cast follows."},
   {n:"The Ninth Seal",d:13,kind:"release"}],
  p2:[{n:"Mulberry Veil",kind:"stance",st:"flow",text:"The sweetness closes over the hall like weather.",tele:"The veil gathers \u2014 flow again, deeper."},
   {n:"Needle-script, running hand",d:8,drain:2},
   {n:"Drawing the tithe",kind:"heal",h:5,text:"She drinks another season of her own banked self.",tele:"Filaments brightening again \u2014 Snare the draw."},
   {n:"The Ninth Seal",d:11,kind:"release"}]}});


SC["a4c26_convene"]={t:()=>SYS(`CHAPTER TWENTY-SIX — SUYIN'S CHOICE`)+P(`The Reels convene at dawn, and it is the strangest court you have ever stood in, because every party to it is sincere.`)+P(`The convening hall crowns the city's central tower: white, round, open to the sky, ringed by nine great reels and the seats of their officers — seven attending in person, the Seventh's seat conspicuously empty since the document-house, and the First present the way weather is present: in every reel at once. Your company stands with you.`)+((G.f.a4_audit=="published")?(P(`Beyond the lake, you can almost feel it: three river sects reading the Court's own arithmetic this morning in Yan's sealed hand. The Court can feel it too. The hall's politeness has edges today.`)):(P(`Under three sects' wax, downriver, the full audit sits sealed, and every officer in this hall knows you hold it, which gives the morning's politeness a financial quality.`)))+P(`You hang the model warp in the center of the hall, forty lines and a handspan of held sky, and you make the argument of your life. Suyin's forty years. Ruan's checked figures. The watch-rota. The load per shoulder, lighter than a market-day's carry. The heat-budget read aloud — ninety parts in a hundred burned to keep dead pattern supple — and at THAT figure, you watch two of the younger Reel-officers stop breathing, because they are believers, and believers can be wounded by a true number in a way no enemy ever can.`)+P(`The First Reel listens from everywhere. When you finish — the model holding, the hall silent — her voice comes level as ever, and very old.`)+P(`“Four hundred years,” she says, “I asked for a competent wrongness. Show me the knot.”`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Tie the Sage's Shuttle in the model, in front of all of them.`,go:"a4c26_shuttle"}]};

SC["a4c26_shuttle"]={t:()=>P(`You tie it the way you learned it: from inside.`)+P(`Gold runs down into the model warp and you go WITH it, a line among lines, and in front of nine reels and seven officers and your own assembled family, you tie the knot the old books call impossible: the pattern that includes its weaver, self-tensioning, alive. The model's forty lines take up the new design in one soft chord, the dead lines sloughing, the willing ones singing, and the handspan of sky holds with no furnace, no fuel, no heat at all: a piece of heaven, mended, on nothing but consent.`)+P(`In the silence afterward, the First Reel's voice has something in it four centuries old and brand new.`)+P(`“So. There IS a fourth truth.” A long turning of reels. “Hear the Court's finding: the model is sound. The scale is not proven. The crossover is an open gap in a held sky, and the holder of that gap dies unwitnessed if your tying runs slow. And the sky of the heartland is not a model, little stitch, and I have not been wrong yet at the only sum that counts. The Court will permit the attempt —” the reels stop, all of them, everywhere, one heartbeat of total stillness — “at the season's turn. Six weeks. Prove your scale by then, gather your willing thread by then, and the warp is yours to retie. I have held four hundred years. I can hold six more weeks, and I would so prefer to be wrong before I fray.”`)+P(`The hall does not get to exhale. Because that is when the teacup, at the ring's edge, is set down with a click that stops the room.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Madam Xian rises.`,go:"a4c26_doorway"}]};

SC["a4c26_doorway"]={t:()=>P(`She stands between you and the hall's great door, in hostess white, and she is past argument; you can read it in her filaments before she speaks. Believers can be wounded by a true number. They can also refuse the wound.`)+P(`“Lady,” she says, to everywhere, “you taught me the sum when I was nine years old. A thousand souls a generation, against the sky. I have TITHED to that sum forty years, gladly. And you would let a boy unpick it on six weeks and a parlor model.” Her gaze comes to you, and it is not hostile; it is bereaved. “If the gap fails, Lady, you do not get to be wrong QUIETLY. The sky falls on ten thousand villages. Somebody must be willing to be damned to prevent it. The Seventh tried crudely. I am not crude.”`)+P(`The First Reel's voice, even now, does not rise: “Ninth. Stand down. The finding is given.”`)+P(`“The finding is GAMBLED,” Madam Xian says, and bows to the everywhere voice with perfect love, and disobeys it. White thread begins to run off her sleeves in quantities the hall's reels lean toward.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`She has read your file since before the brackets. Let her read your arithmetic instead.`,req:()=>(G.insight>=16 && G.f.a3_believer),rq:"(needs Insight 16 and her tithe read, from the white boat)",do:()=>{G.f.a4_xian="turned";},go:"a4c26_talk"},
  {id:"c1",l:`“You taught me the politeness, Madam. It's going to hurt one of us.”`,go:"a4c26_ninth"}]};

SC["a4c26_talk"]={t:()=>P(`You don't fight her. You out-account her.`)+P(`“Forty years of tithe,” you say, and her filaments hesitate, because you are reading them aloud in front of her Lady. “Paid in continuously, willingly, out the hull of a white boat down the river to the lake country. I saw it at our first tea: you pay IN, Madam. You always have. So run the audit with me, Ninth Reel: the Loom burned ninety parts of every soul it was ever fed, and banked your forty years against — what? Say the figure. You've never once dared total your own column.”`)+P(`She is silent. The hall's reels are silent.`)+P(`“The model isn't unpicking your sum. It's the only design in four hundred years where your tithe BUYS what you've been paying for. Willing thread, holding sky, no furnace eating nine-tenths of the gift. You are not the Court's objection, Madam Xian. You are the counter-pattern's PROOF. You have been all along. The Lady's whole machine never managed to spend you, because you were never fuel: you were structure the old Loom had no slot for.”`)+P(`The white thread settles back onto her sleeves, one filament at a time, the way snow decides against a storm. When she bows — to you, to her Lady, to the arithmetic, no one in the hall can say which — it is the deepest anyone has seen the Ninth Reel bow, and the most frightening thing you have seen her do, and this time it is on your side of the ledger.`)+P(`“Six weeks,” she says, hostess-smooth again, ruinously quiet. “I will bring the first rota myself. The Court does not lie, weaver. It appears it merely... mislaid a column.” She steps out of the doorway.`)+SYS(`The Ninth Reel turns. Madam Xian — first officer of the willing rota. (a4_xian: turned)`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Which leaves only the gap, and the question of who holds it.`,go:"a4c26_choice"}]};

SC["a4c26_ninth"]={combat:"xian",
 win:"a4c26_yield",
 lose:"a4c26_fallen",
 t:()=>P(`The hall clears with the discipline of people who have rehearsed disasters for four centuries. The First Reel does not intervene, and you understand, mid-breath, that this TOO is the finding: a Court of believers settles doctrine by what survives. Madam Xian pours toward you like the white boat coming to take everything back.`)};

SC["a4c26_fallen"]={t:()=>P(`She does not finish it. Of course she doesn't.`)+P(`You wake on the convening floor with your threads rung out like bells and Madam Xian kneeling beside you, hostess to the last, setting your limbs straight with professional tenderness. “The gap would have spent you in a quarter hour,” she says, conversationally. “That is the lesson, weaver, and I am content it was taught by tea-room sparring rather than the sky. Take it and the Court takes nothing else today.”`)+SYS(`Defeat teaches: +1 Insight. The argument is not over; it has merely seen your floor. Grasp the thread and stand again.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Stand. The model still hangs in the hall, still holding its handspan of heaven.`,do:()=>{addIns(1);if(CKPT)G=JSON.parse(CKPT);},go:"a4c26_ninth"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Yield the bout, keep the finding. Six weeks stands; the Ninth remains unpersuaded, and unforgiven.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_xian="stood";},go:"a4c26_choice"}]};

SC["a4c26_yield"]={t:()=>P(`It is the hardest fight of your life, because she is forty years of paid-in self with a believer's whole heart behind it, and because neither of you hates the other, which removes every shortcut.`)+P(`When it ends — her last seal-cast counterwoven mid-air, gold running through the white and the white admitting, line by line, that it holds — she yields the way Sister Lacquer yielded: completely, instantly, the sum gone against her and the new total accepted whole. She sits down on the convening floor amid her own settling silk, breathing hard, and begins, of all things, to laugh: a small, scandalized, decades-late sound.`)+P(`“Ninety parts in a hundred,” she says. “Forty years, and I never totaled my own column.” She looks up at you, hostess-eyes clear. “Six weeks, weaver. I will bring the first rota myself. It appears I have been structure all along, mislaid in the fuel ledger. The Court does not lie. It is, however, capable of the most extraordinary filing errors.”`)+SYS(`The Ninth Reel yields — and turns. Madam Xian, first officer of the willing rota. (a4_xian: turned)`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`Which leaves only the gap, and the question of who holds it.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_xian="turned";},go:"a4c26_choice"}]};

SC["a4c26_choice"]={t:()=>P(`That evening, in the warp-gallery, the question gets its answer, and the answer was never yours to give.`)+((G.f.a4_unmarked && G.sho>=3)?(P(`Suyin has already begun. You feel it from the stair: a slow, deliberate slackening in the province's chord — forty years of woven self, paying itself OUT, line by patient line, her own fan unweaving under her own hands at the pace of a long exhale. Granny Sho stands beside her, hands on the warp, taking each freed line's load for the moment it needs a shoulder, the resonance the recruiters wrote about forty years ago finally doing the one job it was always for.`)+P(`“The claim is off my sister's shoulder,” Suyin says, working. “The audit is out of the Court's drawer. And the gap, stitch, must be held by someone FREE: the old books are plain, I finally checked: a holder still woven into the dying pattern goes down with it. So.” A line frees; Sho catches it; the two of them sway like one tree. “I am tearing out. Six weeks early, forty years late. I will hold your gap as a free woman, with my sister on the lines beside me, and when the new sky sings I intend to be OUTSIDE it, eating riverbank plums.”`)+P(`The First Reel's voice, from one small reel by the stair, almost gentle: “Warp-elder. The province will feel every line of this.” “Then hold it with me, Lady,” Suyin says, silk over iron. “Six weeks. You said you could.”`)):(""))+((G.f.a4_unmarked && G.sho<3)?(P(`Suyin hears you out — the gap, the holder, the risk of the tying running slow — and is quiet for the length of one full splice. Then: “It must be held by someone who knows the heart-position as a body knows a bed. Forty years, stitch. There is one of those.” You start the argument she's been waiting for; she stops it with one raised, thread-laced hand. “I held a courtyard's sky at nineteen with no training and no choice. Let me hold this one with both. It is not a debt, child. It is the same arithmetic I have always done, finally pointed at the right answer.” (a4_suyin: holds)`)):(""))+((!G.f.a4_unmarked)?(P(`Suyin hears you out, and then she looks at you — Pattern Sage to Pattern Sage, the only two alive — and reads the thing you'd buried under the plan's clean lines: the claim still written on a beloved shoulder, the leash you kept “for cover,” the hour of gold you've been carrying like a stone. “You meant to trade yourself into the gap,” she says, not a question. “Hold it yourself, spend yourself, and call the books balanced. The prisoner's arithmetic; I know it; I WROTE it, forty years ago on a courtyard.” Her hands take yours, thread-laced, unrefusable. “No, stitch. The pattern needs its weaver OUTSIDE the gap, tying. The gap needs a holder who knows the position. That is me. That was always me. The only question left is whether you'll waste our six weeks arguing with the one person who can read your sleeve.”`)):("")),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`The arithmetic is hers, and it has never once come out different. Accept it, and spend the six weeks making the tying FAST.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_suyin=(G.f.a4_unmarked&&G.sho>=3)?"freed":"holds";addIns(1);note("+1 Insight. You finally understand what Granny Sho meant on the boat: don't let me be cruel to her for surviving. Surviving IS her craft. You stop arguing with forty years of it, and the plan gets honest.");},go:"a4c26_verdict"},
  {id:"c1",l:`Offer yourself anyway: out loud, formally, so it's on the Court's record that someone tried.`,do:()=>{G.f.a4_suyin=(G.f.a4_unmarked&&G.sho>=3)?"freed":"holds";G.heart++;note("+1 Heart. Suyin lets you finish the whole offer, witnessed, and then declines it with the gentlest sentence ever recorded in the Court's minutes: \"The Loom remembers its stitches, child \u2014 and I remember mine. Sit down.\" The record keeps both. Some offers are made to be refused and matter anyway.");},go:"a4c26_verdict"}]};

SC["a4c26_verdict"]={t:()=>P(`Six weeks, then. The act ends the way the white city does everything: on schedule.`)+P(`The rota gathers ahead of every estimate — Madam Xian${G.f.a4_xian=="turned"?" recruiting with a convert's terrifying efficiency":" abstaining with glacial correctness while her junior officers defect to the rota in twos and threes"}; resonants arriving on every tide, miller's daughters and bridge-keepers and one entire fishing village from two bays west of nowhere, forty roofs' worth, who heard the weaver needed shoulders. Yan drills the signal-order. Bao builds the supply line. Mei stocks a field-infirmary at the warp-gallery's mouth and dares anyone to call it pessimism. Ruan audits the rota's load-tables until they are beyond reproach, and then audits them again, for the pleasure.`)+P(`And on the last evening of the fifth week, the First Reel speaks to you alone, from the small black reel in the shrine-niche, in a voice that has put away the everywhere-ness, and sounds, for the first time, like one tired woman.`)+P(`“I have held this sum four hundred years, little stitch. Next week I find out what I bought and what I merely COST.” The reel turns once. “Finish your pattern. Tie it fast and tie it true, because if your gap gapes one breath too long, I will do what I have always done. I will take the sky's weight back, with every soul in reach, and I will not be sorry, and we will not speak again as friends.” A pause, dry as winter leaves, eerily like a broom on stairs. “And if you SUCCEED, weaver — be kind to the machine you retire. She did hold. Whatever else is true of her, for four hundred years, she held.”`)+SYS(`ACT FOUR CLOSES. The model is proven, the rota is gathered, the gap has its holder, and the season turns in seven days. What remains is the tying, and the tying is Act V.`),
 c:()=>[{id:"c0",l:`There is one more place to stand before the crossover: the center of the Loom, where the world's weave touches its selvage. Suyin calls it the door's porch.`,go:"a5c27_door"}]};